      ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ and the block diagonal matrix $B$ shown below, where the $2\\times 2$ block of $B$ represents a rotation-scaling matrix:\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5+7\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i}\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are the eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1-2\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=-2,$  respectively. \nGiven that $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ which of the following could be the matrix $P?$"
